{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Behold, I have acquired you this day.</b> The reason he said <b>this day</b> — he also inserted the word היום (\"this day\") to distinguish between their acquisition and the acquisition of the land. For their acquisition is by means of drawing, according to the law of acquiring slaves (Kiddushin 22b), and the deed he performed — transferring the people to the cities from one end, etc. — that constitutes their acquisition. Therefore he said <b>Behold, I have acquired you this day</b>, meaning, through transferring them then to the cities. But as for the land, that is not the method of its acquisition; and when he mentioned above ״וַיִּקֶן יוֹסֵף אֶת אַדְמַת מִצְרַיִם״ (v. 20), there it is hinted that he acquired it by one of the methods of acquiring land." "<b>And there is</b> room to raise another difficulty: once he acquired them, what need was there for acquiring their land? Is it not so that whatever a slave acquires, his master acquires (Pesachim 88b)? Perhaps it is because their acquisition was not like the acquisition of slaves, but rather was specified for the purpose of working the land, etc., and giving a fifth to Pharaoh — this is nothing but like the acquisition of a hired laborer, who does not acquire full ownership. And therefore he needed to acquire the land, and he acquired it by complete acquisition, as the verse revealed in saying: ״וַיִּקֶן יוֹסֵף אֶת כָּל אַדְמַת מִצְרַיִם וְגוֹ׳ כִּי מָכְרוּ מִצְרַיִם אִישׁ שָׂדֵהוּ״ (v. 20). And if Pharaoh wished to bring laborers and work the land for his own benefit and ownership, he may do so — unlike the persons of the Egyptians, concerning whom he did not say he acquired by complete acquisition. And even though he said ״הֵן קָנִיתִי אֶתְכֶם״, this means like the acquisition of a hired laborer for the matter mentioned in Joseph's words: ״הֵא לָכֶם זֶרַע״ etc. (v. 23). And Joseph's reasoning was: what good is the land if there is no one to work it? Therefore he was wise to acquire them, to obligate them for the labor."], :book :genesis, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:49:40.574226770Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}